{
 "record": "K005: order of simultaneous events in the Metrica proxy labels (records correction; no selection affected)",
 "written_at": "2026-11-11T17:31:43+03:00",
 "finding": "Three reporting-only records were scored against Metrica proxy labels that had lost about half of their dead-ball intervals: the full-size rehearsal of K003 (bundles A and B), the slot / duplicate diagnostic of K003 and the goalkeeper diagnostic that motivated K004. They had been run in the Python 3.10 environment of the release (pandas 2.1.4, numpy 1.26.4); every selection, gate, validation and reserved test ran in the experiment environment (Python 3.13, pandas 3.0.5, numpy 2.5.3), where the labels are as intended.",
 "how_it_was_found": "In the full-size rehearsal of possession-v2.11 (K004) the bundle with exchanged goalkeeper ids, built in the experiment environment, scored higher than bundle A of K003, although both have the same content. Their label files differed in 17,448 frames, all of them H or A in bundle A and D in the new bundle.",
 "cause": "experiments/possession_v2/metrica_labels.labels_from_events sorted the events by 'Start Frame' with the default sort, which is not stable. In the provider's files a SET PIECE and the PASS that takes it share a start frame, and the dead-ball interval before a restart is recorded only if the SET PIECE row stays first, as in the file. Under pandas 3.0.5 / numpy 2.5.3 the default sort keeps the file order of these ties (identical to a stable sort on all three games); under pandas 2.1.4 / numpy 1.26.4 it does not.",
